  "content": "Given a rectangle with perimeter $P = 30$ and length $L = 9$, the perimeter formula is $P = 2(L + W)$. Substituting the known values:\n\n$$30 = 2(9 + W)$$\n\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\n$$15 = 9 + W$$\n\nSubtract 9 from both sides to find the width:\n\n$$W = 15 - 9 = 6$$\n\nThe area $A$ is calculated as $A = L \\times W$:\n\n$$A = 9 \\times 6 = 54$$\n\n**Width:** 6\n**Area:** 54",
  "reasoning": "",
